            <ArticleTitle>Anti-Inflammatory Activity of Phyllanthus singampattiyana. Leaf Extract.</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>296-298</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <ELocationID EIdType="doi" ValidYN="Y">10.1080/13880200590951667</ELocationID>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>We studied the anti-inflammatory activity of a petroleum ether extract of Phyllanthus singampattiana. Sebastine and A.N. Henry leaves, which was tested in Wistar rats with TPA-induced ear inflammation and carrageenan-induced paw edema. Carrageenan-induced paw edema was significantly reduced at a dose of 100 mg petroleum ether extract (p &lt; 0.05%). From the crude extract, β.-sitosterol was identified and confirmed.</AbstractText>
            </Abstract>
